From 2c5469e6f66a12dc654664c0a1678f8112de912b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] texts: what keeping disks away does not hold against, with
 what the start runs

The start runs post-flash.sh, mount-storage.sh and post-sysroot.sh where they
are on the partition LIBREELEC, before the internal disks are kept away, and
installs an update left in /storage, which is the system of the next start.
A program that writes them can undo keeping disks away from the next start,
as one that changes the list or the boot menu can: what keeping disks away
means says so.
---
 resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po | 2 +-
 resources/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po | 4 ++--
 resources/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po | 4 ++--
 resources/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po | 4 ++--
 4 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
index 7a5b1ad..00e0181 100644
--- a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
+++ b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
@@ -1569,7 +1569,7 @@ msgid "Every internal disk is shown from the next start"
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#33157"
-msgid "With disks kept away, from the next start:[CR][CR]- Before anything else runs, this system lets go of the disks that are not ticked. Kodi, its add-ons and file sharing do not see them, and neither can a program that runs here with full rights reach them.[CR][CR]- The kernel attaches no other internal disk until the next start: a disk that is plugged in while the system runs is seen from the next start.[CR][CR]- The kernel runs with its lockdown, as in the normal start: it loads only the drivers that came with this system, not the ones that add-ons bring, and keeps programs away from the memory and the hardware of the computer.[CR][CR]- A disk with no serial number, or with the same one as another disk, cannot be told apart from others, so it is kept away too, and every disk is kept away when the list cannot be read. The disk this system is on is never kept away.[CR][CR]- Where a disk that is to be kept away cannot be (the system cannot let go of it, or cannot tell which disk it starts from), it stays, and no partition of an internal disk is mounted in that start. That is said when Kodi starts.[CR][CR]- It holds against what runs in this system, until the next start. It does not hold against a program that changes this list or the boot menu and waits for the next start.[CR][CR]- It is so on every computer that this drive is started on: their disks go with the first line of the list."
+msgid "With disks kept away, from the next start:[CR][CR]- Before anything else runs, this system lets go of the disks that are not ticked. Kodi, its add-ons and file sharing do not see them, and neither can a program that runs here with full rights reach them.[CR][CR]- The kernel attaches no other internal disk until the next start: a disk that is plugged in while the system runs is seen from the next start.[CR][CR]- The kernel runs with its lockdown, as in the normal start: it loads only the drivers that came with this system, not the ones that add-ons bring, and keeps programs away from the memory and the hardware of the computer.[CR][CR]- A disk with no serial number, or with the same one as another disk, cannot be told apart from others, so it is kept away too, and every disk is kept away when the list cannot be read. The disk this system is on is never kept away.[CR][CR]- Where a disk that is to be kept away cannot be (the system cannot let go of it, or cannot tell which disk it starts from), it stays, and no partition of an internal disk is mounted in that start. That is said when Kodi starts.[CR][CR]- It holds against what runs in this system, until the next start. It does not hold against a program that changes this list, the boot menu or what the system runs as it starts (scripts on the partition LIBREELEC, an update in /storage), and waits for the next start.[CR][CR]- It is so on every computer that this drive is started on: their disks go with the first line of the list."
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#33158"
